.TH GHID 1 "2026-10-22" "GhostHID 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ghid \- Headless Android Bluetooth HID Keyboard Controller & Automation Gateway
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ghid
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-s\fR \fIserial\fR] [\fIcommand\fR] [\fIarguments...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ghid
is the command-line interface for the GhostHID platform. It converts
a rooted or standard Android phone connected via USB or Wireless ADB
into a fully programmatic, headless Bluetooth HID (Human Interface
Device) keyboard for a target Windows laptop or PC.
.PP
Unlike software-based remote-control agents, GhostHID operates at the
Bluetooth hardware host controller layer (Bluetooth HID Device Profile
/ SDP). The target computer recognizes the phone as a physical,
driverless peripheral keyboard.
.PP
When invoked without arguments in an interactive terminal,
.B ghid
launches an interactive console that monitors device status, connects
to the target machine, and exposes actions for automated login, screen
locking, system sleep, typing, and diagnostic health checks.
.PP
For AI agents and automated scripts, all commands can be invoked
non-interactively and support the
.B \-\-json
flag for structured, machine-readable output.

.SH HARDWARE & BLUETOOTH BEHAVIOR NOTE
.B Wake-on-Bluetooth limitation:
When the target Windows laptop is in ACPI sleep (Modern Standby / S3),
the host's Bluetooth controller is unpowered and cannot receive
Bluetooth packets. The target laptop must be manually awakened
(e.g. tapping the physical power button or a key on the laptop's
built-in keyboard).
.PP
Once the laptop is awake, running
.B ghid
will automatically connect the phone's HID profile over Bluetooth
L2CAP channels within 1\(en2 seconds.

.SH INTERACTIVE WORKFLOW
When launched interactively:
.IP 1. 4
.B ADB & Device Verification:
Detects connected Android devices. If no device is detected, presents
an interactive recovery menu offering to connect to configured
Wireless ADB endpoints, scan for USB devices, or pair a new device
using an Android pairing code.
.IP 2. 4
.B APK Validation:
Checks if \fIcom.sj010.ghid_headless\fR is installed on the device. If missing,
prompts to install the pre-compiled APK or build it directly from
source via \fIbuild.sh\fR.
.IP 3. 4
.B Bluetooth HID Gateway:
Ensures the phone's Bluetooth radio is enabled, starts the foreground
Android service, and negotiates SDP registration.
.IP 4. 4
.B Target Link:
Connects to the paired target laptop Bluetooth address.
.IP 5. 4
.B Action Menu:
Provides numbered actions:
.RS 8
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlogin\fR: Authenticates with Windows using cached macOS Keychain credentials.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlock\fR: Sends instant Win+L keystroke sequence.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsleep\fR: Dispatches Win+X \(-> u \(-> s sleep sequence, begins a countdown,
disconnects Bluetooth, and terminates background phone services.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtype\fR: Prompts for arbitrary text and injects it character-by-character.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcombo\fR: Sends shortcuts (e.g. \fIctrl+alt+del\fR, \fIwin+d\fR, \fIalt+tab\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBraw\fR: Transmits raw 8-byte HID reports.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcreds\fR: Inspects or updates cached credentials in macOS Keychain.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBreconnect\fR: Re-establishes dropped Bluetooth connection.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBexit\fR: Disconnects target and terminates phone foreground service.
.RE

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B devices \fR[\fBlist\fR | \fBadd\fR | \fBselect\fR | \fBdelete\fR]
Manage registered target Bluetooth devices (Windows PCs or Apple Macs).
.RS
.TP
\fBlist\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
List all registered devices with active indicator and platform badge.
.TP
\fBadd\fR \fB\-\-name\fR \fIname\fR \fB\-\-addr\fR \fImac\fR [\fB\-\-os\fR \fIwindows|macos\fR] [\fB\-\-select\fR]
Register a new device into the config and optionally activate it immediately.
.TP
\fBselect\fR \fItarget\fR
Switch the active target device by ID, name, or MAC address,
and initiate connection.
.TP
\fBdelete\fR \fItarget\fR [\fB\-f\fR]
Unregister a device from configuration and unpair Bluetooth bonding on phone.
.RE
.TP
.B interactive \fR(alias: \fBi\fR)
Launch interactive terminal user interface (default in a TTY).
.TP
.B status \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Display current Android gateway and Bluetooth connection status.
Exits with 0 if connected to target, 1 otherwise.
.TP
.B start
Start Android foreground service (\fIHidService\fR) and register
SDP profile.
.TP
.B stop
Disconnect Bluetooth and stop the Android foreground service.
.TP
.B restart
Restart the Android foreground service.
.TP
.B connect \fR[\fIaddress\fR]
Initiate Bluetooth HID connection to target laptop. If \fIaddress\fR is omitted,
uses the saved address in configuration.
.TP
.B disconnect
Disconnect active Bluetooth HID session.
.TP
.B unpair
Remove Bluetooth pairing bond with target laptop from phone.
.TP
.B login \fR[\fB\-u\fR \fIusername\fR] [\fB\-p\fR \fIpassword\fR] [\fB\-\-save\fR] [\fB\-f\fR]
Execute automated Windows login sequence:
.RS
1. Send Ctrl+Alt+Delete to wake lock screen
.br
2. Send Escape to clear lock screen overlay
.br
3. Type Username
.br
4. Send Tab key
.br
5. Type Password
.br
6. Send Enter key
.RE
If credentials are not provided via arguments,
.B ghid
checks the macOS Keychain for stored credentials. In interactive mode,
it will prompt for missing values and offer to cache them.
.TP
.B lock
Instantly send Windows lock shortcut (\fIWin + L\fR).
.TP
.B sleep \fR[\fB\-\-countdown\fR \fIsecs\fR] [\fB\-\-no-exit\fR]
Dispatches Windows sleep sequence (\fIWin+X\fR \(-> \fIu\fR \(-> \fIs\fR).
Begins countdown timer (default: 5 seconds), then cleanly disconnects
Bluetooth and stops Android gateway service so that zero background
battery drain occurs.
.TP
.B type \fItext...\fR
Type arbitrary string arguments through virtual keyboard.
.TP
.B combo \fR[\fIkeys\fR | \fBlist\fR | \fBsave\fR | \fBsend\fR | \fBdelete\fR | \fBmouse\fR]
With no arguments, opens the interactive Windows Combo Studio: saved combos
are listed (or an empty-state card is shown), \fBEnter\fR sends the selected
combo, \fBTab\fR focuses the SEND / NEW / DELETE buttons, \fBn\fR creates a
named combo, and \fBDelete\fR removes one after a Y/N confirmation.
.PP
.RS 4
\fBghid combo list\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] \- list saved combos.
.br
\fBghid combo schema\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] \- grammar and every accepted token.
.br
\fBghid combo validate\fR \fIkeys...\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] \- parse without
saving or sending; exits 1 when invalid.
.br
\fBghid combo save\fR \fIname\fR \fIkeys...\fR \- save a named combo.
.br
\fBghid combo send\fR \fIname\fR \- send a saved combo.
.br
\fBghid combo delete\fR \fIname\fR [\fB\-f\fR] \- delete with confirmation.
.br
\fBghid combo\fR \fIkeys\fR \- one-shot send (e.g. \fIwin+d\fR).
.br
\fBghid combo mouse\fR \fIgesture\fR \- \fIclick-left\fR, \fIclick-right\fR,
\fIclick-middle\fR, \fIdouble-click\fR, \fIscroll-up\fR, \fIscroll-down\fR.
.RE
.PP
Keyboard tokens cover real Windows keys: \fIwin\fR, \fIctrl\fR, \fIalt\fR,
\fIshift\fR, \fIa\fR\(en\fIz\fR, \fI0\fR\(en\fI9\fR, \fIf1\fR\(en\fIf12\fR,
\fIenter\fR, \fIesc\fR, \fItab\fR, \fIspace\fR, \fIbackspace\fR, \fIdel\fR,
\fIinsert\fR, navigation keys, \fIprintscreen\fR, \fIcapslock\fR,
\fInumlock\fR, \fIscrolllock\fR, \fIpause\fR, \fImenu\fR and punctuation names
such as \fIsemicolon\fR or \fIslash\fR. Type literal text with a
\fBtype:\fR step: \fIwin+s ->{0.7} type:rustdesk ->{0.3} enter\fR (quote text
with spaces as \fItype:"rust desk"\fR; printable ASCII only). Chain steps with
\fI->{seconds}\fR, for example \fIwin+r ->{0.6} click-left\fR. macOS-only
aliases (\fIcmd\fR, \fIsuper\fR, \fIoption\fR) are rejected.
.PP
The combo library is stored in \fI~/.config/ghid/combos.json\fR. The mouse uses
HID report ID 2, so re-pair the phone on Windows after updating the APK.
.PP
For automation, \fB\-\-json\fR makes every combo command non-interactive:
errors are emitted as JSON on stdout with exit code 1, and \fBcombo delete\fR
skips the confirmation prompt. Use \fBcombo schema \-\-json\fR to enumerate
supported keys and gestures, then \fBcombo validate\fR before \fBcombo save\fR.
.TP
.B raw \fIhex16\fR
Send raw 8-byte (16 hex character) USB HID keyboard report.
Byte 0 is modifier bitmap, Byte 1 is reserved (0x00), Bytes 2\(en7
are keycode array.
.TP
.B creds \fR{\fBstatus\fR|\fBset\fR|\fBclear\fR} [\fB\-u\fR \fIuser\fR] [\fB\-p\fR \fIpass\fR]
Manage stored login credentials inside secure macOS Keychain
(service: \fIghost-hid\fR).
.TP
.B doctor \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Run comprehensive diagnostic sweep checking ADB availability, device
connection, package installation, phone Bluetooth state, SDP profile
registration, target laptop connectivity, and macOS Keychain accessibility.
.TP
.B install-apk \fR[\fB\-\-path\fR \fIapk\fR] [\fB\-\-build\fR]
Install or update GhostHID application APK onto target Android device.
.TP
.B build
Compile Android APK from source using standalone toolchain in \fIbuild.sh\fR.
.TP
.B logs \fR[\fB\-n\fR \fIlines\fR]
Dump most recent log entries filtered for GhostHID from device \fIlogcat\fR.
.TP
.B tail
Stream real-time GhostHID logs from phone.
.TP
.B filelog
Display persistent event log written to
\fI/sdcard/Android/data/com.sj010.ghid_headless/files/gateway.log\fR on phone.
.TP
.B install-bin \fR[\fB\-\-dir\fR \fIpath\fR]
Symlink \fBghid\fR into \fI~/.local/bin\fR and install man page into
\fI~/.local/share/man/man1\fR.
.TP
.B uninstall-bin
Remove installed binary symlink and man page.
.TP
.B man
Display this manual page using system manual viewer.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show program version and exit.
.TP
.B \-s \fIserial\fR, \fB\-\-serial \fIserial\fR
Specify serial number or IP:PORT of Android device to target.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit all output formatted as structured JSON for automation and
AI agent parsing.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (or status is connected).
.TP
.B 1
General error, target disconnected, or diagnostic issue identified.
.TP
.B 2
ADB not found in system PATH or standard Android SDK directories.

.SH FILES & ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.I ~/.config/ghid/config.json
Configuration file holding default target Bluetooth MAC address,
wireless ADB IP, and timing parameters. Permissions are locked to 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/ghid
Default installation symlink path.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/man/man1/ghid.1
Default installed manual page location.
.TP
.B ANDROID_SERIAL
Environment variable specifying default Android device serial.
.TP
.B ADB_PATH
Environment variable pointing to custom \fIadb\fR binary location.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, disables ANSI color output.

.SH EXAMPLES
.IP \(bu 2
Start interactive session:
.RS 6
.B ghid
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
Check gateway status in JSON format (AI agent mode):
.RS 6
.B ghid status --json
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
Run comprehensive system health check:
.RS 6
.B ghid doctor --json
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
Unlock Windows laptop using cached Keychain credentials:
.RS 6
.B ghid login
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
Unlock Windows laptop specifying explicit username and password:
.RS 6
.B ghid login -u Administrator -p SecretPass123
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
Lock Windows screen immediately:
.RS 6
.B ghid lock
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
Put Windows laptop to sleep and cleanly exit gateway:
.RS 6
.B ghid sleep --countdown 5
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
Type arbitrary text:
.RS 6
.B ghid type "Hello, Windows!"
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
Send shortcut combination:
.RS 6
.B ghid combo "win+r"
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
Send raw HID keyboard report:
.RS 6
.B ghid raw 08000f0000000000
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
Store Windows credentials in macOS Keychain:
.RS 6
.B ghid creds set -u Administrator -p SecretPass123
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
Install ghid executable symlink and man page:
.RS 6
.B ghid install-bin
.RE

.SH TROUBLESHOOTING & RECOVERY
.TP
.B Target laptop asleep and will not connect:
Wake-on-Bluetooth is not supported when target laptop is in low-power
sleep states. Tap physical keyboard or power button on laptop,
then run \fBghid\fR or select \fB[8] reconnect\fR.
.TP
.B No device connected:
Ensure phone is connected via USB with USB debugging enabled, or
connected over Wi-Fi using \fBadb connect <ip>:<port>\fR.
.TP
.B APK missing:
Run \fBghid build\fR followed by \fBghid install-apk\fR.

.SH SEE ALSO
